><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: Prevention of ankle sprains and ACL rupture should be a prior-ity. The use of a neuromuscular warm-up such as the NetballAustralia ‘KNEE’ program should be considered.•Foot blisters are common but can be prevented with load man-agement, appropriate footwear, good hygiene and prophylactictaping.•Implementation planning of injury prevention interventionsmust be prioritised.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
